---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Will I still be able to use Cursor, Lovable, or Bolt to build features after the rescue?',
    answer: 'Absolutely. A core goal of our rescue sprint is to structure your codebase into clean, modular files with clear type interfaces and comprehensive schema documentation. We also provide an "AI Prompting & System Guide" so your AI coding assistants can continue building new features without corrupting database policies or auth layers.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How do you handle intellectual property (IP) and security confidentiality?',
    answer: 'All work is performed under a strict bilateral Non-Disclosure Agreement (NDA). You maintain 100% ownership of all code, architecture, and documentation created. We only request least-privilege GitHub collaborator access and never store or train models on your proprietary logic.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What if my vibe-coded prototype is "too broken" or spaghetti code?',
    answer: 'In 95% of prototypes, the frontend UI and business flow are solid—the breakage is isolated to authentication, database security policies, asynchronous race conditions, or build pipelines. During the 48-Hour Diagnostic, I give you a transparent assessment. If the codebase is genuinely unfixable, I will tell you directly.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How does the 100% Money-Back Guarantee work?',
    answer: 'If the 48-Hour Production Readiness Audit does not deliver actionable, high-severity security, architecture, or performance remediation items that protect your application, your audit fee is refunded in full. No hurdles or questions asked.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How quickly can we start, and what is the turnaround time?',
    answer: 'Code Diagnostics start within 24 hours of booking and are delivered within 48 hours. Rescue Sprints typically start the following Monday and run for 1 to 2 weeks depending on scope.'
  },
  {
    question: 'I am a non-technical founder. Will you explain everything in plain English?',
    answer: 'Yes! Our entire service is tailored for non-technical founders, solo creators, and operators. Every report and video walkthrough focuses on business risks, customer security, payment reliability, and launch readiness—not abstract academic jargon.'
  }
];
---

<section id="faq" class="border-b border-ink">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-20 lg:py-24">

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-26">

      <div>
        <p class="text-small font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-signal mb-5">
          Frequently Asked Questions
        </p>
        <h2 class="text-[2.25rem] sm:text-[2.75rem] lg:text-section text-ink">
          Everything You Need to Know About <span class="text-signal">Vibe Code Rescue.</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-6 text-body text-ink max-w-[480px]">
          Have questions before booking your triage? Here are answers to common questions from founders.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-10 pt-8 border-t border-ink max-w-[480px]">
          <h3 class="text-sub text-ink">Have a unique scenario or urgent launch blocker?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink">
            We can review your architecture live on a screen share today.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6">
            <a href="#triage" class="ghost-link">Book a Free 15-Min Code Triage</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-ink">
        {faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details class="group border-b border-ink [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-start justify-between gap-6 py-6 text-body font-bold text-ink list-none">
              <span>{faq.question}</span>
              <!-- Plus turns to minus: two ink bars, one rotates away -->
              <span class="relative shrink-0 w-4 h-4 mt-2" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="absolute inset-x-0 top-1/2 h-[2px] -translate-y-1/2 bg-ink"></span>
                <span
                  class="absolute inset-x-0 top-1/2 h-[2px] -translate-y-1/2 bg-ink rotate-90 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-0"
                ></span>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="pb-6 -mt-1 text-body text-ink max-w-[480px]">{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
